= Astronomy
{wiki}

Astronomy studies celestial objects and phenomena. <Astrometry> measures their positions and motion; <astrophysics> uses <physics> to explain their properties and behaviour.

= Astrometry
{parent=Astronomy}
{wiki}

Astrometry measures the positions and motions of celestial objects. Repeated position measurements can distinguish <stellar parallax>, caused by the observer's motion, from <proper motion> of the source across the sky.

= Proper motion
{parent=Astrometry}
{title2=$\mu$}
{wiki}

Proper motion describes the change in a celestial object's direction on the sky due to its motion relative to the observer. Its angular rate differs from the annual <stellar parallax> signal caused by the observer's orbit.
